{
  "contract": "evidence-transport/v1 and evidence-exchange/v1 checkpoint handoff order and stop projections",
  "warning": "The secret below is the published ingest test value and must never authenticate anything real.",
  "note": "checkpoint_sequences replay one identity's runtime and gateway: `produce` seals an artifact, `drain` hands off everything eligible, `ack` is a verified `queued` acknowledgement and `ack_lost` one the runtime never received. `handed_off` lists a drain's handoffs in order, `gateway_order` the gateway's admitted order, `local_waiting` the checkpoints the gateway has never admitted and that are neither stopped nor refused, `local_stopped` the unacknowledged artifacts in a stopped scope, and `delivery_failures` the checkpoints whose verified terminal admission refusal the runtime durably recorded (`recorded`; `authenticated: false` marks an acknowledgement or refusal that did not verify); `custody_move` moves the runtime's stored copy of a checkpoint out of the active offer loop into `damaged` or `foreign_identity` custody, `durable` saying whether the move committed, and `moved_custody` lists the checkpoints so moved. stop_cases are projections with the request's device and the digests of the authority artifacts the same response carries; stop_sequences apply them to a gateway queue, where `stopped` lists covered entries, `order` the queue order, `archived` what was archived, `sendable` what the courier may still send, and `registration_slot_free` the devices whose reserved registration slot no active entry occupies. `retained_bytes`, `active_bytes` and `stopped_bytes` are the gateway's retained byte totals, `entries` its count of retained entries in both states, and `interrupt_after` a crash after that many covered entries have moved. In a stop sequence, `admit` is a later outbound admission of `entry`, and `admission` says whether it entered the active queue (`queued`), stopped custody (`stopped_custody`), or no custody at all (`no_custody`, with no acknowledgement); `stopped_bound` is the per-device and total stopped-custody item bound in force, set on the sequence or lowered by a `gateway_restart`, and `faults` carries `stopped_custody_full` while stopped custody is at or above a bound. `artifact_type` names an admitted entry's outbound type, and `effects` lists, in order, what a stopped-scope admission makes durable and publishes: `stopped_bytes_durable` once the stopped bytes and their return obligation are durable, `custody_acknowledgement_staged` once a delivery envelope's custody acknowledgement is durably staged, and `queued` when the outbound acknowledgement is published; it is empty for an admission that receives no custody.",
  "secret": "published-test-evidence-ingest-secret-with-256-bit-entropy-do-not-use",
  "key_id": "hkdf-sha256:169ab7dc3fdf30297687df61205d72ac",
